    pr_ref:  # 7d65
    description: "**Defect.** The reproducibility fingerprint over-captures grammar versions for languages that produced zero nodes.\n\n**Evidence.** `reproducibility_context.captured.grammars` enumerates 51 installed tree-sitter grammar versions (agda, circom, cuda, fortran, julia, lean, zig, ...) regardless of whether each grammar was used. Only 17 languages are actually present in the nodes; 38 of the 51 captured grammars correspond to languages with zero nodes. The implications text then asserts that maps with matching per-grammar versions should be functionally identical.\n\n**Contract.** The fingerprint should capture only grammars that actually contributed to the output (or the \"functionally identical\" implication should be scoped to used grammars), so that environment changes which cannot affect the map do not appear to.\n\n**Consequence.** The fingerprint conflates \"grammar installed\" with \"grammar used\"; a consumer diffing the captured block for reproducibility sees spurious \"not functionally identical\" verdicts driven by grammar versions for languages the repo does not contain.\n\n**Related (not duplicate).** Distinct from WI-mifok (pass_versions absent from captured) — this is over-capture of unused grammars, not absence of a referenced field."  # 7d65
    fields: {}  # 7d65
